  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Secure Document Sharing",
    "description": "• Worked with a team to complete the project by the deadline\n• Implemented OAuth2 Authentication server\n• Implemented end-to-end encryption using RSA and AES\n• Used Docker to host the application and setup automatic deployment of newer versions of the application\n• Used Caddy to setup a reverse proxy to the Spring Boot application and TLS for the API\n• Used Quartz Job Scheduler to schedule automatic deletion of documents that expire",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jun 2021 - Dec 2021"
   },
   {
    "title": "Sudoku Solver",
    "description": "This is a project that shows off my ability to implement algorithms and display a visual of what is happening while the algorithm is being run. The Sudoku Solver utilizes C# for the algorithm and the display of data through the use of SFML.NET.\n\nThe goal of this project was to get me to be more comfortable in a few different areas of programming:\n- Implementing an algorithm to solve a real world puzzle without the use of initial tutorials\n- Using an OpenGL GUI interface without the use of software like Unity\n- Using threads and keeping things thread safe\n- Creating software that can work cross-platform and actually testing them to ensure that they work with the same code base.\n- Properly including the licenses to different third party libraries that I utilize",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Dec 2019 - Dec 2019"
   }
